<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>Brightcove Streaming Inspector v3.1</title>
  <style>
    :root{
      --bg:#070b10;
      --panel:#0d131b;
      --line:rgba(255,255,255,.11);
      --line-2:rgba(255,255,255,.18);
      --text:#edf3fb;
      --muted:#9aa7b8;
      --soft:#c9d4e1;
      --gold:#f4d24b;
      --cyan:#77d4ff;
      --green:#65e0a3;
      --amber:#ffcb6b;
      --red:#ff8f8f;
      --shadow:0 18px 48px rgba(0,0,0,.35);
      --radius-xl:24px;
      --radius-lg:18px;
      --mono:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;
      --sans:Inter,ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',sans-serif;
    }
    *{box-sizing:border-box}
    html,body{margin:0;padding:0}
    body{
      min-height:100vh;
      font-family:var(--sans);
      color:var(--text);
      background:
        radial-gradient(circle at top left, rgba(244,210,75,.13), transparent 22%),
        radial-gradient(circle at top right, rgba(119,212,255,.12), transparent 24%),
        linear-gradient(180deg, #06090e 0%, #070b10 100%);
    }
    .shell{max-width:1380px;margin:0 auto;padding:28px 22px 72px}
    .hero{
      position:relative;overflow:hidden;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius-xl);
      background:
        linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(244,210,75,.16), rgba(255,111,97,.12) 38%, rgba(119,212,255,.16)),
        linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(255,255,255,.05), rgba(255,255,255,.03));
      box-shadow:var(--shadow);padding:22px 22px 20px;margin-bottom:20px;
    }
    .hero-row{display:flex;align-items:flex-start;justify-content:space-between;gap:18px}
    .eyebrow{display:inline-block;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#fff5b1;font-weight:800}
    .hero h1{margin:8px 0 8px;font-size:clamp(30px,4vw,46px);line-height:1.04;letter-spacing:-.03em}
    .hero p{margin:0;max-width:940px;color:#e8eef8;opacity:.9;line-height:1.7;font-size:15px}
    .hero-pill{
      align-self:flex-start;white-space:nowrap;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.14);
      background:rgba(17,27,39,.3);border-radius:999px;padding:10px 14px;color:#f2f6fc;font-size:13px;
    }
    .grid-main{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.06fr .94fr;gap:20px}
    @media (max-width:1120px){.grid-main{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
    .panel{
      border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius-xl);
      background:linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(255,255,255,.05), rgba(255,255,255,.025)), #0b1017;
      box-shadow:var(--shadow);overflow:hidden;
    }
    .panel-head{padding:18px 20px 0;display:flex;align-items:flex-start;justify-content:space-between;gap:16px}
    .panel-title{margin:0;font-size:21px;letter-spacing:-.02em}
    .panel-sub{margin:6px 0 0;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.65;font-size:14px}
    .panel-badge{
      flex:0 0 auto;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.12);border-radius:999px;padding:8px 12px;
      font-size:12px;color:#eff4fb;background:rgba(255,255,255,.04);font-family:var(--mono)
    }
    .panel-body{padding:18px 20px 20px}
    .form-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr)) auto;gap:12px;align-items:end}
    @media (max-width:980px){.form-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
    .field label{
      display:block;margin:0 0 8px;font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--soft)
    }
    .field input{
      width:100%;appearance:none;border:1px solid var(--line-2);background:rgba(255,255,255,.03);color:var(--text);
      border-radius:14px;padding:14px 14px;font:inherit;outline:none
    }
    .actions{display:flex;gap:10px;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap}
    .btn{
      appearance:none;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.12);cursor:pointer;border-radius:14px;padding:14px 16px;
      font:inherit;font-weight:800;color:#0b1117;background:linear-gradient(135deg, var(--gold), #ffe58f)
    }
    .btn.secondary{background:rgba(255,255,255,.04);color:var(--text)}
    .summary-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(5,minmax(0,1fr));gap:12px;margin-top:6px}
    @media (max-width:1180px){.summary-grid{grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr))}}
    @media (max-width:800px){.summary-grid{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}}
    @media (max-width:560px){.summary-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
    .metric{
      border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:18px;padding:14px 14px 13px;
      background:linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(244,210,75,.12), rgba(255,111,97,.08) 42%, rgba(119,212,255,.12)), rgba(255,255,255,.025)
    }
    .metric .k{margin:0 0 6px;color:#fff4b1;font-size:11px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.09em;text-transform:uppercase}
    .metric .v{margin:0;font-size:20px;line-height:1.2;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:-.02em;overflow-wrap:anywhere}
    .metric .h{margin:8px 0 0;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;color:#d0dae6;min-height:2.8em}
    .status-good{color:var(--green)} .status-warn{color:var(--amber)} .status-bad{color:var(--red)} .status-info{color:var(--cyan)} .status-plain{color:var(--text)}
    .player-wrap{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.16fr) minmax(320px,.84fr);gap:18px}
    @media (max-width:1120px){.player-wrap{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
    .player-stage{
      border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:20px;
      background:radial-gradient(circle at top left, rgba(119,212,255,.09), transparent 26%), radial-gradient(circle at bottom right, rgba(244,210,75,.09), transparent 24%), #070d13;
      overflow:hidden;min-height:360px;position:relative;
    }
    .player-stage .player-slot{aspect-ratio:16/9;width:100%;min-height:360px;display:grid;place-items:center}
    .placeholder{padding:24px;text-align:center;color:var(--muted);font-family:var(--mono);line-height:1.8;font-size:13px}
    .info-stack{display:grid;gap:12px}
    .mini{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:18px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.03);padding:14px}
    .mini .k{margin:0 0 6px;color:var(--soft);font-size:11px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.09em;text-transform:uppercase}
    .mini .v{margin:0;font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--text);overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word;font-family:var(--mono)}
    .mini .s{margin:7px 0 0;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.65;font-size:13px}
    .note{border-left:3px solid rgba(244,210,75,.75);padding-left:12px;margin-top:12px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;font-size:14px}
    .flow-panel{margin-top:20px}
    .flow-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(6,minmax(0,1fr));gap:12px;align-items:stretch}
    @media (max-width:1180px){.flow-grid{grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr))}}
    @media (max-width:720px){.flow-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
    .flow-step{
      position:relative;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:18px;padding:14px;
      background:linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(244,210,75,.08), rgba(255,111,97,.05) 40%, rgba(119,212,255,.08)), rgba(255,255,255,.02)
    }
    .flow-step .n{margin:0 0 6px;color:#fff4b1;font-size:11px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.09em;text-transform:uppercase}
    .flow-step .t{margin:0 0 6px;font-size:22px;line-height:1.15;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:-.03em;overflow-wrap:anywhere}
    .flow-step .d{margin:0;font-size:13px;line-height:1.65;color:#d0dae6}
    .log{
      margin:0;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:18px;background:#04080d;color:#dbe6f2;padding:14px;
      font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12px;line-height:1.75;min-height:340px;max-height:520px;overflow:auto;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word
    }
    .log-row{display:block;padding:0 0 8px;border-bottom:1px dashed rgba(255,255,255,.06);margin-bottom:8px}
    .tag{
      display:inline-block;min-width:72px;text-align:center;margin-right:10px;border-radius:999px;padding:4px 8px;
      font-size:11px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.1);vertical-align:top
    }
    .tag.info{background:rgba(119,212,255,.12);color:#a7e5ff}
    .tag.good{background:rgba(101,224,163,.11);color:#9eecbf}
    .tag.warn{background:rgba(255,203,107,.12);color:#ffd78d}
    .tag.bad{background:rgba(255,143,143,.12);color:#ffb3b3}
    .explain{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:12px;margin-top:4px}
    @media (max-width:900px){.explain{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
    .footer-note{margin-top:12px;color:var(--muted);font-size:12px;line-height:1.8;font-family:var(--mono)}
    .video-js, video-js{width:100% !important;height:100% !important;display:block}
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="shell">
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="hero-row">
        <div>
          <div class="eyebrow">Brightcove Streaming Inspector</div>
          <h1>DRM</h1>
          <p>Load any Brightcove player by Account ID, Player ID, and Video ID, then inspect the stream with a simplified DRM-first summary: <strong>DRM Signal</strong>, <strong>DRM System</strong>, <strong>License Exchange</strong>, <strong>License Latency</strong>, and <strong>Protected Playback</strong>.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-pill">drm-first view</div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="grid-main">
      <section class="panel">
        <div class="panel-head">
          <div>
            <h2 class="panel-title">Run Inspector</h2>
            <p class="panel-sub">Use customer-specific account, player, and video IDs. This keeps the tool account-agnostic and suitable for troubleshooting.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="panel-badge">dynamic player loader</div>
        </div>
        <div class="panel-body">
          <div class="form-grid">
            <div class="field">
              <label for="accountId">Account ID</label>
              <input id="accountId" type="text" placeholder="e.g. 123456789001" />
            </div>
            <div class="field">
              <label for="playerId">Player ID</label>
              <input id="playerId" type="text" placeholder="e.g. default or your custom player ID" />
            </div>
            <div class="field">
              <label for="videoId">Video ID</label>
              <input id="videoId" type="text" placeholder="e.g. 1234567890001" />
            </div>
            <div class="actions">
              <button class="btn" id="runBtn" type="button">Run Inspector</button>
              <button class="btn secondary" id="clearBtn" type="button">Clear</button>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="summary-grid">
            <div class="metric">
              <p class="k">DRM Signal</p>
              <p class="v status-plain" id="metricDrmSignal">Not observed</p>
              <p class="h" id="hintDrmSignal">No DRM signal observed yet.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="metric">
              <p class="k">DRM System</p>
              <p class="v status-plain" id="metricDrmSystem">Unknown</p>
              <p class="h" id="hintDrmSystem">Widevine, FairPlay, or PlayReady will appear here when detected.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="metric">
              <p class="k">License Exchange</p>
              <p class="v status-plain" id="metricLicense">Not observed</p>
              <p class="h" id="hintLicense">A real DRM license request usually appears after playback begins.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="metric">
              <p class="k">License Latency</p>
              <p class="v status-plain" id="metricLatency">Unknown</p>
              <p class="h" id="hintLatency">Shown when a DRM-style license request/response is observed.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="metric">
              <p class="k">Protected Playback</p>
              <p class="v status-plain" id="metricProtectedPlayback">Unknown</p>
              <p class="h" id="hintProtectedPlayback">Best signal: encrypted event or confirmed key/license flow plus playback.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="note">This v3.1 summary keeps the headline UX focused on what most users actually care about: Is DRM configured, what DRM system is involved, did a license exchange happen, how long did it take, and did protected playback succeed?</div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="panel">
        <div class="panel-head">
          <div>
            <h2 class="panel-title">How to read this page</h2>
            <p class="panel-sub">This tool is optimized for support and onboarding, not for replacing the full browser Network tab.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="panel-badge">support mode</div>
        </div>
        <div class="panel-body">
          <div class="explain">
            <div class="mini">
              <p class="k">Step 1</p>
              <p class="v">DRM configured</p>
              <p class="s">Manifest signal or DRM-specific request pattern indicates that the stream is intended to be protected.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="mini">
              <p class="k">Step 2</p>
              <p class="v">License exchange</p>
              <p class="s">A POST request to a license-style endpoint is a strong sign that the player is negotiating keys.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="mini">
              <p class="k">Step 3</p>
              <p class="v">Protected playback</p>
              <p class="s">Playback plus EME/DRM signals usually means the content is playing through a protected path.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>

    <section class="panel" style="margin-top:20px;">
      <div class="panel-head">
        <div>
          <h2 class="panel-title">Player & Runtime</h2>
          <p class="panel-sub">The Brightcove player is created dynamically from the IDs you enter above.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="panel-badge">runtime view</div>
      </div>
      <div class="panel-body">
        <div class="player-wrap">
          <div class="player-stage">
            <div class="player-slot" id="playerContainer">
              <div class="placeholder">Player slot is waiting for input.<br />Enter Account ID, Player ID, and Video ID, then click <strong>Run Inspector</strong>.</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="info-stack">
            <div class="mini">
              <p class="k">Player Script URL</p>
              <p class="v" id="scriptUrlValue">Not loaded yet</p>
              <p class="s">This is the Brightcove player runtime script that will be loaded dynamically.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="mini">
              <p class="k">Player URL Pattern</p>
              <p class="v" id="playerUrlValue">Not loaded yet</p>
              <p class="s">Useful for comparing direct player access with in-page playback or iframe-based playback.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="mini">
              <p class="k">Observed Page Context</p>
              <p class="v" id="pageContextValue">Waiting for player load</p>
              <p class="s">Shows where the current page itself is running, which helps when explaining runtime context.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="mini">
              <p class="k">Player Status</p>
              <p class="v" id="playerStatusValue">Idle</p>
              <p class="s">Tracks dynamic load, player readiness, and playback lifecycle hints.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="footer-note">Note: browser security and DRM implementation differences mean some details can only be reported as observed, likely, or unknown.</div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="panel flow-panel">
      <div class="panel-head">
        <div>
          <h2 class="panel-title">How DRM playback actually starts</h2>
          <p class="panel-sub">License requests usually do not happen when the player first loads. In most cases, they happen after playback begins and the browser detects encrypted media.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="panel-badge">play → license → key → playback</div>
      </div>
      <div class="panel-body">
        <div class="flow-grid">
          <div class="flow-step">
            <p class="n">1</p>
            <p class="t">Player loads</p>
            <p class="d">The Brightcove player script loads and the player requests the manifest.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="flow-step">
            <p class="n">2</p>
            <p class="t">User presses play</p>
            <p class="d">The browser starts actual playback startup work instead of only loading the player UI.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="flow-step">
            <p class="n">3</p>
            <p class="t">Encrypted media is detected</p>
            <p class="d">The browser or player encounters DRM-protected media and starts the EME path.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="flow-step">
            <p class="n">4</p>
            <p class="t">License request is sent</p>
            <p class="d">The CDM generates a challenge and the player sends it to the DRM license server.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="flow-step">
            <p class="n">5</p>
            <p class="t">License response returns keys</p>
            <p class="d">The license server returns data the browser can use to unlock decryption for that session.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="flow-step">
            <p class="n">6</p>
            <p class="t">Protected playback starts</p>
            <p class="d">Once usable keys are installed, encrypted media segments can be decrypted and playback can continue.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="note" style="margin-top:16px;"><strong>Why license latency matters:</strong> because the license exchange usually happens during playback startup, a slow or overloaded license server can directly increase startup delay or cause playback failures.</div>

        <div class="mini" style="margin-top:16px;background:linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(244,210,75,.06), rgba(119,212,255,.06)), rgba(255,255,255,.02);">
          <p class="k">Visual Handshake Model</p>
          <p class="s" style="margin-top:0;">This SVG shows the typical communication path after the user presses play. It is not a packet-level trace; it is a support-friendly model of how protected playback usually starts.</p>

          
